<title>UK: IFC sets 10 bln yen dual-currency three-year bond.</title>
<headline>IFC sets 10 bln yen dual-currency three-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Kankaku (Europe) and DKB International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   INTERNATIONAL FINANCE CORP</p>
<p> AMT    10 BLN YEN    COUPON    *5.35	MATURITY    09.DEC.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    09.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.50	REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	 =</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 100 (M) 1 GOV LAW     NEW YORK</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES     *REDEMPTION IN AUSTRALIAN DOLLARS.</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
